questions.question_text:
$\triangle DEF$ has been reflected in the dashed mirror line to give the second triangle.
Which congruence statement is correct?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (D) at (0,0);
\coordinate (E) at (2.4,0.2);
\coordinate (F) at (0.7,1.5);
\coordinate (L) at (6.0,0);
\coordinate (K) at (3.6,0.2);
\coordinate (M) at (5.3,1.5);
\draw (D) -- (E) -- (F) -- cycle;
\draw (L) -- (K) -- (M) -- cycle;
\draw[dashed] (3.0,-0.5) -- (3.0,2.0);
\node[below left] at (D) {$D$};
\node[below right] at (E) {$E$};
\node[above] at (F) {$F$};
\node[below right] at (L) {$L$};
\node[below left] at (K) {$K$};
\node[above] at (M) {$M$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Quadrilateral $EFGH$ has been translated to give the second quadrilateral.
Which congruence statement is correct?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (E) at (0,0);
\coordinate (F) at (2.2,0);
\coordinate (G) at (1.7,1.4);
\coordinate (H) at (0.4,1.4);
\coordinate (P) at (3.4,0.4);
\coordinate (Q) at (5.6,0.4);
\coordinate (R) at (5.1,1.8);
\coordinate (S) at (3.8,1.8);
\draw (E) -- (F) -- (G) -- (H) -- cycle;
\draw (P) -- (Q) -- (R) -- (S) -- cycle;
\node[below] at (E) {$E$};
\node[below] at (F) {$F$};
\node[above] at (G) {$G$};
\node[above] at (H) {$H$};
\node[below] at (P) {$P$};
\node[below] at (Q) {$Q$};
\node[above] at (R) {$R$};
\node[above] at (S) {$S$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$\triangle BDF$ has been reflected in the dashed mirror line to give the second triangle. Which vertex corresponds to $D$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) node[below left] {$B$} -- (2.4,0) node[below right] {$D$} -- (0.7,1.5) node[above] {$F$} -- cycle;
\draw (6,0) node[below right] {$K$} -- (3.6,0) node[below left] {$M$} -- (5.3,1.5) node[above] {$H$} -- cycle;
\draw[dashed] (3,-0.4) -- (3,2);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$\triangle PRT$ has been rotated through a half turn to give the second triangle. Which side corresponds to side $PT$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) node[below left] {$P$} -- (2.5,0) node[below right] {$R$} -- (0.8,1.6) node[above] {$T$} -- cycle;
\draw (6,1.6) node[above right] {$E$} -- (3.5,1.6) node[above left] {$G$} -- (5.2,0) node[below] {$C$} -- cycle;
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Quadrilateral $KLMN$ has been reflected in the dashed mirror line to give the second quadrilateral. Which angle corresponds to $\angle M$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) node[below left] {$K$} -- (2.4,0) node[below right] {$L$} -- (1.8,1.5) node[above right] {$M$} -- (0,1.5) node[above left] {$N$} -- cycle;
\draw (6,0) node[below right] {$X$} -- (3.6,0) node[below left] {$Y$} -- (4.2,1.5) node[above left] {$Z$} -- (6,1.5) node[above right] {$W$} -- cycle;
\draw[dashed] (3,-0.4) -- (3,2);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The second triangle is a rotation of the first. Which congruence statement is correct?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) node[below left] {$G$} -- (2.6,0) node[below right] {$H$} -- (0.6,1.7) node[above] {$K$} -- cycle;
\draw (5.5,0) node[below right] {$R$} -- (5.5,2.6) node[above] {$P$} -- (3.8,0.6) node[left] {$Q$} -- cycle;
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The triangles are congruent. The second is a rotation of the first. Which answer gives a correct congruence statement and the size of $\angle WYX$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) node[below left] {$C$} -- (2.6,0) node[below right] {$D$} -- (0.8,1.8) node[above] {$E$} -- cycle;
\node at (0.5,0.3) {$72^{\circ}$};
\node at (2,0.3) {$57^{\circ}$};
\draw (6,0) node[below right] {$X$} -- (6,2.6) node[above] {$Y$} -- (4.2,0.8) node[left] {$W$} -- cycle;
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Diagrams are not drawn to scale.

The quadrilaterals are congruent. The second is a half turn of the first. Which answer gives a correct congruence statement and the length of $EF$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) node[below left] {$D$} -- (2.8,0) node[below right] {$E$} -- (2.3,1.5) node[above right] {$F$} -- (0.4,1.9) node[above left] {$G$} -- cycle;
\draw (6.5,1.9) node[above right] {$T$} -- (3.7,1.9) node[above left] {$R$} -- (4.2,0.4) node[below left] {$U$} -- (6.1,0) node[below right] {$S$} -- cycle;
\node[above] at (5.1,1.9) {$6.5\text{ cm}$};
\node[left] at (3.95,1.15) {$9.5\text{ cm}$};
\node[below] at (5.15,0.2) {$7.5\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Diagrams are not drawn to scale.
